---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Modern documentation for Agent Runtime." />
    <title>Agent Runtime — Durable agent infrastructure</title>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: light dark; font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; }
      body { margin: 0; background: Canvas; color: CanvasText; }
      main { margin: 0 auto; max-width: 76rem; padding: 8rem 2rem 6rem; }
      h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6.8rem); letter-spacing: -0.065em; line-height: .94; max-width: 15ch; }
      p { font-size: 1.25rem; max-width: 48rem; }
      .eyebrow { color: #5b4ff7; font-size: .76rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .18em; }
      .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .8rem; margin: 2rem 0 4rem; }
      a { border: 1px solid #5b4ff7; border-radius: .5rem; color: inherit; font-weight: 700; padding: .75rem 1rem; text-decoration: none; }
      a.primary { background: #5b4ff7; color: white; }
      .grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
      article { border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, CanvasText 20%, transparent); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.5rem; }
      article p { font-size: 1rem; }
      @media (max-width: 760px) { main { padding-top: 4rem; } .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <div class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE · DURABLE · EXPLICIT</div>
      <h1>Build agents that can survive the real world.</h1>
      <p>Agent Runtime is a monorepo for durable sessions, governed tools, human approvals, artifacts, and isolated execution.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="primary" href={`${base}docs/start-here`}>Explore the foundation</a>
        <a href={`${base}docs/security/verified-boundaries`}>Read the safety boundary</a>
      </div>
      <section class="grid" aria-label="Project principles">
        <article><h2>Durable by design</h2><p>Sessions and Turns are designed around durable state, resumable observation, and explicit terminal outcomes.</p></article>
        <article><h2>Authority is explicit</h2><p>A model tool call is intent. Policy, approval, capability grants, and recorded execution remain separate.</p></article>
        <article><h2>Evidence before claims</h2><p>The docs distinguish planned architecture from locally verified behavior and Linux/KVM security evidence.</p></article>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
